<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Equus scotti follicular Turing wavelength at 164 µm (Irvingtonian, 0.6 Ma) — Code-to-model traceability: 80/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Each modelling step is a named function tied to a formula in the module docstring and in the math-KG YAML. Loop_3220 proves the sign of the determinant, the trace, the Dv/Du = 20 drive, the equal-diffusion failure, the wavelength order, and the eight-mode count, with no sorry. The integer Jacobian is the 10× scaling of the floating-point entries the script uses." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Equus scotti follicular Turing wavelength at 164 µm (Irvingtonian, 0.6 Ma) — Model fidelity to source: 76/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "schnakenberg_jacobian, sigma_plus, and diffusivity_for_wavelength implement the published Jacobian and define k_c as argmax sigma_+, which the run places at 164.37 µm. The spectral IMEX step is the same update used for the single-mode growth test. Murray's determinant stationary point is computed separately (130.6 µm) and not confused with k_c. The equal-diffusion failure and the predecessor/successor diffusivities are stated in the Lean file and the reference JSON but are not executed." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_3220_equus_scotti_turing_wavelength_s0.lean L28–L34: Equal-diffusion Turing condition is proved and not yet run in the script <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/613cdbbd89d39feb2d3ec526d962fb10569c7a9c/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_3220_equus_scotti_turing_wavelength_s0.lean#L28-L34>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Equus scotti follicular Turing wavelength at 164 µm (Irvingtonian, 0.6 Ma) — Morphometric validation: 74/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "IMEX growth versus analytical sigma_+ gives Pearson r = 0.99341 (reference 1) and RMSE = 0.037 (reference 0) on the 32 real-eigenvalue wavenumbers. The nonlinear radial-FFT wavelength is 167.94 µm against the assigned 164.3 µm, so the comparison is not a copy of the reference. Complex-eigenvalue wavenumbers are excluded and counted. There is no KS test and no measurement on the specimen image." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "models/2026-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0.py L344–L388: Four measurements; specimen KS and coherency absent <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/613cdbbd89d39feb2d3ec526d962fb10569c7a9c/models/2026-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0.py#L344-L388>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-dispersion-rmse>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-equus-scotti-nonlinear-stripe-wavelength>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-imex-vs-analytical-dispersion-pearson-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-mature-pattern-standard-deviation-versus-homogeneous-steady-state>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Equus scotti follicular Turing wavelength at 164 µm (Irvingtonian, 0.6 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 74.6/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 implements Schnakenberg kinetics, places k_c = argmax sigma_+(k) at 164.3 µm (measured linear peak 164.37 µm; nonlinear radial-FFT peak 167.94 µm; Murray stationary wavelength 130.6 µm), and fits IMEX single-mode growth to the analytical dispersion at Pearson r = 0.993. The Horsfall 1905 public-domain restoration is the specimen. The script does not sweep Pliohippus or Equus quagga, does not run Du = Dv, and does not segment the plate. Overall 74.6/100 (faithfulness 71.2, reproducibility 82.4); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 613cdbbd89d39feb2d3ec526d962fb10569c7a9c; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 76, Morphological realism / specimen match 71, Parameter expressivity 58, Morphometric validation 74, Source and data traceability 86, Code-to-model traceability 80, Reproducibility package 81. Output judged: docs/media/equus_scotti_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 613cdbbd89d39feb2d3ec526d962fb10569c7a9c, image/png, 716619 B, 1344×1008 px, artifact_sha256 96a6b63b9b9a616b306da698fb23124098ce9900488df16ffdf3a45c06fb21c0 (sha256 96a6b63b9b9a616b306da698fb23124098ce9900488df16ffdf3a45c06fb21c0), spec_fingerprint a3ff127a4fbe604c383fca881bbb59ca1298842374b9b9112403cb1ca2e31003. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: a3ff127a4fbe604c383fca881bbb59ca1298842374b9b9112403cb1ca2e31003; artifact_sha256: 96a6b63b9b9a616b306da698fb23124098ce9900488df16ffdf3a45c06fb21c0. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: diffusion-driven instability and a dispersion relation for chemical wavelength selection. | Schnakenberg 1979: activator-substrate kinetics du/dt and dv/dt with the u^2 v nonlinearity. | Bard 1977: zebra initiation spacing about 0.4 mm, fixed at different embryonic weeks; week 3 for the plains-zebra / quagga pattern. | Murray 1981: coat mode count is set by domain size relative to the chemical wavelength. | MacFadden 1986: equid body size increases from Hyracotherium to Equus.; reconstructed_in_script: Du and Dv at Dv/Du = 20 are solved so argmax sigma_+ equals 2*pi/164.3 µm. | The predecessor wavelength 198.7 µm is the focal wavelength times the catalog linear-size ratio 0.260/0.215. It is not a measured Pliohippus coat spacing. | The flank ocelli are a visualization of the 164 µm field on a whole-animal plate.; transfer_boundary: 164.3 µm is the assigned phenomenon scale of slot 3220, not a length measured on an Equus scotti fossil. | Equus chronoseries 1/2 (scotti then quagga) is the campaign order. Scotti is a North American caballoid; quagga is a zebra.; does_not_claim: That a 164 µm stripe was measured on Equus scotti. | That the Horsfall drawing's pencil grain is a melanocyte field. | That Equus scotti is the direct ancestor of Equus quagga.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Add the equal-diffusion negative control Du = Dv and report that the maximum growth rate for k > 0 is negative.",
        "remediation needed: Extend goodness-of-fit with a KS statistic between the specimen radial spectrum and the simulated radial spectrum, and keep Pearson r and RMSE on the dispersion curve.",
        "remediation needed: Segment the Horsfall plate (foreground fraction, structure-tensor coherency, radial spectrum) and compare those measurements with the simulated activator. Do not score a metric whose value is copied from its reference.",
        "remediation needed: Sweep the chronoseries: Pliohippus pernix at 198.7 µm (Dv/Du = 12), Equus scotti at 164.3 µm (Dv/Du = 20), Equus quagga at the Bard 1977 initiation spacing of 400 µm (Dv/Du = 30), and show that the selected wavelength moves monotonically." ;
    pk:hasScore 7.46e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Equus scotti follicular Turing wavelength at 164 µm (Irvingtonian, 0.6 Ma) — Parameter expressivity: 58/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "One kinetic point is exercised: a=0.10, b=0.90, Dv/Du=20, target 164.3 µm. The diffusivity solver is monotone in the target wavelength, but the script never varies Dv/Du, the predecessor 198.7 µm target, or the Bard 400 µm successor target, so a reader cannot see the wavelength move." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "models/2026-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0.py L213–L252: run_science reads a single parameter row and simulates one patch <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/613cdbbd89d39feb2d3ec526d962fb10569c7a9c/models/2026-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0.py#L213-L252>" ;
    pk:hasScore 5.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Equus scotti follicular Turing wavelength at 164 µm (Irvingtonian, 0.6 Ma) — Reproducibility package: 81/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "--self-test checks the Turing inequalities, the linear peak within 1 µm of 164.3, Pearson r > 0.98, a non-equal nonlinear wavelength, and a GIF of at least 12 frames at least 480 px on the short side. The seed is 3220. Dataset hashes are verified before the solve. The self-test does not yet assert the ablation or the chronoseries." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
