<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Equus scotti follicular Turing wavelength at 164 µm (Irvingtonian, 0.6 Ma) — Morphological realism / specimen match: 71/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The specimen is Horsfall's 1905 public-domain restoration, SHA-256 pinned, shown beside the activator and as a feathered flank overlay in the comparison figure and in a 12-frame GIF (960×649). The overlay is visibly an ocellus field, feathered so the torso window is not a hard rectangle. No measurement is taken from the plate itself: foreground, coherency, and the radial spectrum of the drawing are not compared with the simulation. The plate is a whole animal; 164 µm is below its resolution, and the figure says so." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "models/2026-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0.py L344–L388: measure_morphoeval has no specimen-image segmentation <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/613cdbbd89d39feb2d3ec526d962fb10569c7a9c/models/2026-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0.py#L344-L388>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.1e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Equus scotti follicular Turing wavelength at 164 µm (Irvingtonian, 0.6 Ma) (Equus scotti)",
        "Equus scotti follicular Turing wavelength at 164 µm (Irvingtonian, 0.6 Ma) faithfully reproduces Equus scotti morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Equus scotti specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Equus scotti" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That Equus scotti is the direct ancestor of Equus quagga.",
        "does_not_claim: That a 164 µm stripe was measured on Equus scotti.",
        "does_not_claim: That the Horsfall drawing's pencil grain is a melanocyte field.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Du and Dv at Dv/Du = 20 are solved so argmax sigma_+ equals 2*pi/164.3 µm.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: The flank ocelli are a visualization of the 164 µm field on a whole-animal plate.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: The predecessor wavelength 198.7 µm is the focal wavelength times the catalog linear-size ratio 0.260/0.215. It is not a measured Pliohippus coat spacing.",
        "reported_in_source: Bard 1977: zebra initiation spacing about 0.4 mm, fixed at different embryonic weeks; week 3 for the plains-zebra / quagga pattern.",
        "reported_in_source: MacFadden 1986: equid body size increases from Hyracotherium to Equus.",
        "reported_in_source: Murray 1981: coat mode count is set by domain size relative to the chemical wavelength.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979: activator-substrate kinetics du/dt and dv/dt with the u^2 v nonlinearity.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952: diffusion-driven instability and a dispersion relation for chemical wavelength selection.",
        "transfer_boundary: 164.3 µm is the assigned phenomenon scale of slot 3220, not a length measured on an Equus scotti fossil.",
        "transfer_boundary: Equus chronoseries 1/2 (scotti then quagga) is the campaign order. Scotti is a North American caballoid; quagga is a zebra." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Equus scotti (Middle Pleistocene (Irvingtonian, 0.6 Ma))" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Mammalia (Zootoka)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Equus" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/equus_scotti_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Equus scotti; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952: diffusion-driven instability and a dispersion relation for chemical wavelength selection. | Schnakenberg 1979: activator-substrate kinetics du/dt and dv/dt with the u^2 v nonlinearity. | Bard 1977: zebra initiation spacing about 0.4 mm, fixed at different embryonic weeks; week 3 for the plains-zebra / quagga pattern. | Murray 1981: coat mode count is set by domain size relative to the chemical wavelength. | MacFadden 1986: equid body size increases from Hyracotherium to Equus.; reconstructed_in_script: Du and Dv at Dv/Du = 20 are solved so argmax sigma_+ equals 2*pi/164.3 µm. | The predecessor wavelength 198.7 µm is the focal wavelength times the catalog linear-size ratio 0.260/0.215. It is not a measured Pliohippus coat spacing. | The flank ocelli are a visualization of the 164 µm field on a whole-animal plate.; transfer_boundary: 164.3 µm is the assigned phenomenon scale of slot 3220, not a length measured on an Equus scotti fossil. | Equus chronoseries 1/2 (scotti then quagga) is the campaign order. Scotti is a North American caballoid; quagga is a zebra.; does_not_claim: That a 164 µm stripe was measured on Equus scotti. | That the Horsfall drawing's pencil grain is a melanocyte field. | That Equus scotti is the direct ancestor of Equus quagga.]; phenomenon_size: 2.1 mm (0.00213 m, log10=-2.672 m, tier=6_organ_mm); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 2.1 mm to 3.41 m): 2.1 mm:equus-quagga-bioelectric-polarity, 4.0 mm:equus-quagga-vertex-packing, 7.6 cm:equus-quagga-turing-wavelength, 13.9 cm:equus-quagga-clock-wavefront, 45.1 cm:equus-quagga-morphogen-condensation, 58.9 cm:equus-quagga-flux-canalization, 62.0 cm:equus-quagga-elastic-buckling, 77.0 cm:equus-quagga-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(81)90334-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1017/s0094837300003109>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1469-7998.1977.tb04204.x> ;
    pk:externalAtlasDataset <https://paleobiodb.org/classic/checkTaxonInfo?taxon_name=Equus>,
        <https://www.morphosource.org/Search/index?search=Equus> ;
    pk:fossilLineageGroup "Equid Autopod & Dental Chronospecies" ;
    pk:geologicalAgeMa 6e-01 ;
    pk:geologicalPeriod "Middle Pleistocene (Irvingtonian, 0.6 Ma)" ;
